WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.020
Our next guests aren't your typical Drew-Gooders.

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.890
They made headlines when they spent an entire weekend

3
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:07.750
picking up dog doo-doo

4
00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:10.920
in 20 degree weather

5
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.680
on the streets of Hoboken, New Jersey.

6
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.380
And we've all been there,

7
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.480
out on a stroll and you look down

8
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.960
and someone forgot to clean up after their dog.

9
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.430
And well, if this has ever been you,

10
00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.300
you're going to freak out at what these Drew-Gooders did

11
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.680
to clean up the sidewalks in their neighborhood.

12
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.420
Just take a look.

13
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.222
So this is just one bag.

14
00:00:31.222 --> 00:00:32.557
(plastic bags rustling)

15
00:00:32.557 --> 00:00:33.558
Bag two.

16
00:00:33.558 --> 00:00:36.891
(plastic bags rustling)

17
00:00:38.974 --> 00:00:41.090
(audience applauding)

18
00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:45.563
Please welcome Luis Perez And Nyomie Nievez.

19
00:00:46.505 --> 00:00:47.838
How you doing?

20
00:00:50.588 --> 00:00:52.723
I mean, why do you do what you do?

21
00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:56.070
I mean, pun intended.

22
00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.876
Yeah, right.

23
00:00:57.876 --> 00:00:59.563
Ah, Ross would love that.

24
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.330
So we own a pet care service called Luv on a Harness

25
00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.110 line:15%
in Hoboken, New Jersey.

26
00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:07.860 line:15%
We walk about 5 to 10 dogs at a time.

27
00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:11.260 line:15%
And back in February, we had a really bad snow storm.

28
00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:14.300
So we decided to take initiative in our own hands,

29
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.860
and a few weeks later in March we went to the streets

30
00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.930
and we started picking up some of the dog droppings

31
00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.120
that were left behind.

32
00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:24.230
And we spent about six hours on a Saturday

33
00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:25.360
and six hours on a Sunday,

34
00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:28.190
so 12 combined during both days.

35
00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:32.770
And we picked about 900 bags of dog droppings

36
00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:34.367 line:15%
between both days.

37
00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:35.200 line:15%
Yes.

38
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.117 line:15%
I'm hoping 'cause it was winter, they were hard.

39
00:01:38.117 --> 00:01:39.497
And cold.

40
00:01:39.497 --> 00:01:40.530
And cold.

41
00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:44.290
There's nothing like a nice wet summer dog doo.

42
00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:47.850
I know because I have dogs, and I foster dogs,

43
00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.070
and I've had dogs.

44
00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:50.920
I know gross, but you know what?

45
00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:52.490
I also have babies and guess what?

46
00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:53.864
They poo too.

47
00:01:53.864 --> 00:01:54.740
(audience laughing)

48
00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:58.500
But seriously, like what makes you do

49
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:02.850
what so many people turn away from and won't do?

50
00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.566
Why are you such a good person?

51
00:02:05.566 --> 00:02:07.370
Honestly, it was his idea.

52
00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:09.250
But it basically came down to the point

53
00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:10.850
that we are always walking there.

54
00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:12.150
We live in Hoboken,

55
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.280 line:15%
we work in Hoboken,

56
00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:15.700 line:15%
and it just got to the point that everybody was complaining.

57
00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:17.230 line:15%
And we're more problem-solvers

58
00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:19.720 line:15%
than actual people who just sit there and complain.

59
00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:22.410
So we took the initiative and we went out there.

60
00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.860
Originally it was supposed to be a group of us,

61
00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:25.880
but you know, him and I make a great team.

62
00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:26.713
And we went out there

63
00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:29.260
and we just started picking up the dog droppings.

64
00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:32.110
And you know, it ended up causing such an impact

65
00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:32.943
in the community,

66
00:02:32.943 --> 00:02:35.560
which you know, we were really happy about.

67
00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.230
Yeah, you got yourselves on television.

68
00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.801
I bet everybody was pretty bummed

69
00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:41.360
they didn't show up after that.

70
00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.590
Good things happen to good people.

71
00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:46.147
You picked up 900 bags of droppings.

72
00:02:47.317 --> 00:02:48.529
900.

73
00:02:48.529 --> 00:02:49.850
900 bags!

74
00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.130
Yes, and we actually made such an impact

75
00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:53.630
that the Hoboken Business Alliance,

76
00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:55.880
they contacted us via our social media,

77
00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.290
which is Luv on a Harness,

78
00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:01.760
and basically they said that they installed dogway stations

79
00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:04.028
just because of what we did.

80
00:03:04.028 --> 00:03:04.987
Yes.

81
00:03:04.987 --> 00:03:07.987
(audience clapping)

82
00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:11.280
We have a special message

83
00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:16.060
from the Mayor of Hoboken, New Jersey, Ravi Bhalla.

84
00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.363
Take a look.

85
00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:20.900 line:15%
Hello, I'm Hoboken Mayor Ravi Bhalla.

86
00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.940 line:15%
And today I want to send a special message

87
00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:26.210 line:15%
to Luis Perez and Nyomie Nievez.

88
00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:27.900
It's sort of a pet peeve of mine

89
00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.370
when owners don't clean up after their dogs.

90
00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:31.740
So, the fact that you cleaned up

91
00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:34.740
nearly 900 doggy bags of poop,

92
00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.590
well, it's a load off my mind

93
00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:38.840
and a load off our sidewalks.

94
00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:41.670
You've gone above and beyond your due diligence,

95
00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:44.670
and for that, myself and the city of Hoboken,

96
00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:48.000
we are awarding you with an official proclamation.

97
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.160
Thank you so much, Luis and Nyomie,

98
00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.679
you deserve a big round of applause.

99
00:03:52.679 --> 00:03:55.388
(audience clapping)

100
00:03:55.388 --> 00:03:56.743
That's awesome. That's awesome.

101
00:03:56.743 --> 00:03:58.962
The Mayor. The Mayor.

102
00:03:58.962 --> 00:03:59.950
And to make it official,

103
00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:04.680
we got the proclamation from the Mayor to give to you.

104
00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:05.513
Oh my God.

105
00:04:05.513 --> 00:04:06.346
Nice.

106
00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.370
So hang that on your wall.

107
00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:09.084
Maybe show off to your friends.

108
00:04:09.084 --> 00:04:10.084
Wow. Nice.

109
00:04:11.954 --> 00:04:13.647
Wow, that's amazing.

110
00:04:13.647 --> 00:04:15.970
Call up your friends who didn't show up

111
00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:17.550
and say, we want you to come over

112
00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:20.140
and look at our official proclamation from the Mayor.

113
00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:23.550
And that's not all, our friends at Canidae Pet Food

114
00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:27.830
want to donate $2,500 worth of pet food and snacks.

115
00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:29.980
So you can share with your dogs

116
00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:32.010
that you walk in your neighborhood.

117
00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:33.799
Oh my god, that's awesome.

118
00:04:33.799 --> 00:04:35.730
Thank you so much.

119
00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:38.002
Thank you, this is awesome.

120
00:04:38.002 --> 00:04:39.495
This is fantastic.

121
00:04:39.495 --> 00:04:40.423
This is amazing.

122
00:04:40.423 --> 00:04:42.940
What would you say if your dog goes to the bathroom

123
00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:44.360
and you're hesitant to pick it up,

124
00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.880
or you're being lazy, or you forgot a bag?

125
00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.230
It's be a good neighbor.

126
00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.640 line:15%
Just, you know, take the initiative

127
00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.460 line:15%
and don't have the mentality of that's not mine.

128
00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:56.390 line:15%
You know, it's like, it's not only disgusting,

129
00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:58.150
but it's unsafe for the children

130
00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:00.040
and the elderly people in all the communities.

131
00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.890
And you know, just picking up a little bit

132
00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:03.670
next to, you know, your dogs,

133
00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.770
it's something that could just make an impact.

134
00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:08.240
I think they'll also step in some at another point.

135
00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:11.253
All right, thank you Luis Perez and Nyomie Nievez,

136
00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:16.040
for joining our Dr. Drewlittle hour.

137
00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.060
You are what makes this so special.

138
00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.477
Thank you so much for coming on.

139
00:05:19.477 --> 00:05:21.080
And can we please stay in touch?

140
00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.890
We're going to put you on the website.

141
00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:24.113
Yes. Yes.

142
00:05:24.113 --> 00:05:25.074
Thank you. Thank you.

143
00:05:25.074 --> 00:05:25.907
Put your company on.

144
00:05:25.907 --> 00:05:28.490 line:15%
(upbeat music)

